# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Original asset packs (161 MB) and font downloads.
# Kept on disk as the reproducible source for tools/build_assets.py, but never
# committed: some of them forbid redistributing the art itself.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
_raw/

# Derived asset trees - regenerate with:  python tools/build_assets.py
assets/gfx/
assets/audio/
assets/atlas/

# Build output (Maven)
target/
out/
*.class
*.jar

# Standalone Windows build - rebuild with:  python tools/make_exe.py
# 289 MB of staged assets and a bundled JRE; nothing here is a source.
build/
dist/

# Scratch
tools/__pycache__/
*.pyc

# IDE
.idea/
*.iml
.vscode/
.settings/
.classpath
.project

# OS junk - the very thing we cleaned out of the asset packs
.DS_Store
__MACOSX/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Regenerable dev previews
tools/preview/

# Regenerable review screenshots
review/

# Source packs that arrived as folders of their own, kept out of git for the
# same reason as _raw/ - neither shipped a licence, so they must not be
# redistributed:
#   assets/packs/homeassets/  the Top-Down Character Home pack. tools/make_village.py
#                             reads it to rebuild the house, and tools/build_assets.py
#                             copies its sheets into assets/gfx/tiles/home/.
#   assets/packs/miniworld/   the Sunnyside World pack. tools/make_island.py reads its
#                             GameMaker project to build assets/maps/village.tmx and
#                             the images under assets/gfx/sunnyside/.
# tools/make_exe.py leaves this folder out of the standalone build.
assets/packs/
